orean theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is $r=13.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039331/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd253cba851166676f518089ebbfeb54ce7f25eb04acf86652df16e10824f9a0"} {"question" "q-325168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039331/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "430ff7c720a1034b1607f771961275fd4768d791245511665b132c3e38f030c4"} {"question" "q-325168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039331/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd253cba851166676f518089ebbfeb54ce7f25eb04acf86652df16e10824f9a0"} {"question" "q-325168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039331/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd253cba851166676f518089ebbfeb54ce7f25eb04acf86652df16e10824f9a0"} {"question" "q-280257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The polar equation of the circle that is centered at the origin and that passes through the point $A(2,4)$ is$\\,\\,r=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039331/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd253cba851166676f518089ebbfeb54ce7f25eb04acf86652df16e10824f9a0"} {"question" "q-280257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" 